 "المشروع بيراقب Google Sheet وبيبعت رسالة Telegram مع كل lead جديد. بيفحص كل دقيقة، وبينضّف التليفونات والإيميلات، وبيتخطى المكرر. التشغيل: انسخ .env.example لـ .env، وثبّت الحزم، وشغّل main.py. ولسه مبيدعمش أكتر من شيت.": "The project watches a Google Sheet and sends a Telegram message for every new lead. It checks every minute, cleans phone numbers and emails, and skips duplicates. To run it: copy .env.example to .env, install the packages, and run main.py. It doesn't support more than one sheet yet.",
 "أول خطوة في الإعداد إيه؟": "What's the first setup step?",
 "تنسخ .env.example لـ .env وتحط فيه الـ bot token.": "Copy .env.example to .env and add the bot token.",
 "\"does not support more than one sheet yet\" معناها؟": "What does \"does not support more than one sheet yet\" mean?",
 "لسه مبيشتغلش مع أكتر من شيت، وممكن يدعمه بعدين.": "It doesn't work with more than one sheet right now, but it may support it later.",
 "Bug report على GitHub": "A bug report on GitHub",
 "Title: Export fails when a row contains Arabic text\n\n**Describe the bug**\nWhen I export a report that contains Arabic names, the app crashes and no file is created.\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n1. Add a customer with the name \"محمد\".\n2. Click \"Export to CSV\".\n\n**Expected behavior**\nThe CSV file is created and the name is shown correctly.\n\n**Actual behavior**\nUnicodeEncodeError: 'charmap' codec can't encode characters\n\n**Environment**\nWindows 11, version 1.4.2\n\n**Workaround**\nRemoving Arabic names before exporting works, but this is not a real solution.": "Title: Export fails when a row contains Arabic text\n\n**Describe the bug**\nWhen I export a report that contains Arabic names, the app crashes and no file is created.\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n1. Add a customer with the name \"محمد\".\n2. Click \"Export to CSV\".\n\n**Expected behavior**\nThe CSV file is created and the name is shown correctly.\n\n**Actual behavior**\nUnicodeEncodeError: 'charmap' codec can't encode characters\n\n**Environment**\nWindows 11, version 1.4.2\n\n**Workaround**\nRemoving Arabic names before exporting works, but this is not a real solution.",
 "صِف المشكلة": "Explain the problem",
 "فيه / بيحتوي": "Includes",
 "بيظهر صح": "Displayed properly",
 "الترميز مش قادر يحوّل الحروف": "The encoding can't convert the characters",
 "حل مؤقت": "A temporary fix",
 "التصدير بيقع لما يكون فيه أسماء عربي. المتوقع ملف CSV بالاسم صح، واللي بيحصل خطأ ترميز UnicodeEncodeError. الحل المؤقت إنك تشيل الأسماء العربي، بس ده مش حل فعلي.": "Exporting crashes when there are Arabic names. The expected result is a CSV with the name shown correctly; what happens is a UnicodeEncodeError. The workaround is removing the Arabic names, but that's not a real fix.",
 "إيه غالبًا سبب المشكلة؟": "What's most likely causing the problem?",
 "الملف بيتكتب بترميز Windows الافتراضي (charmap) مش UTF-8. الحل: open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").": "The file is written with Windows' default encoding (charmap) instead of UTF-8. The fix: open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").",
 "ليه قسم Environment مهم؟": "Why does the Environment section matter?",
 "عشان المشكلة ممكن تحصل على Windows بس، أو في إصدار معيّن.": "Because the problem might only happen on Windows, or in a specific version.",
